# Project Structure — {{project.name}}

> Kiro steering: project layout and file organization.

## Solution Structure

```
{{project.name}}/
├── src/
│   ├── {{project.dotnet.namespace}}.Common/        # primitives, contracts — no deps
│   ├── {{project.dotnet.namespace}}.Domain/        # entities, aggregates, domain events — no external deps
│   ├── {{project.dotnet.namespace}}.Application/   # CQRS commands, queries, handlers — depends on Domain + Common
│   ├── {{project.dotnet.namespace}}.Infrastructure/ # persistence, adapters — depends on Application + Domain + Common
│   └── {{project.dotnet.namespace}}.Presentation/  # WPF app — depends on Application + Infrastructure + Common
├── tests/
│   ├── {{project.dotnet.namespace}}.UnitTests/
│   └── {{project.dotnet.namespace}}.IntegrationTests/
├── context/
└── openspec/
```

## Layer Responsibilities

| Layer | Purpose | Key Packages |
|-------|---------|-------------|
| Common | Primitives, contracts | None |
| Domain | Business model | None |
| Application | Use cases | MediatR, FluentValidation |
| Infrastructure | Persistence, adapters | EF Core, Microsoft.Extensions.DI |
| Presentation | WPF UI | CommunityToolkit.Mvvm, MaterialDesignThemes/WPF-UI, MediatR |

## Dependency Rule

Dependencies always point inward. Never outward.
